      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gFDRr",
      "text": "B and E only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c95181ab-8199-4a34-ab9d-6a2ef8287391.png\" style=\"width: 360px; height: 148px;\" /></p><p>The Lorentz force is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>. The angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Hence the force experienced is zero.</p><p>Thus, the electron will not experience any magnetic force and the electron will continue to move along the axis.</p></blockquote>",
